{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790350652,"nonce":"lqTKN5EDPmBCVFY1Ovc7WGkoX8k=","title":"zyntax compile's LLVM AOT output does not link: main is mangled to its id","message":"Since 48bf287 the LLVM backend keeps a function's source name only for the entry names its host configures (set_entry_names) and mangles every other local function to `func_HirId(n)`. compile_llvm (crates/zyntax_cli/src/backends/llvm_aot.rs) never configured any, so `main` was emitted as `func_HirId(3)` and every AOT build failed to link with \"undefined reference to `main'\" (GNU ld) or \"Undefined symbols: _main\" (ld64), whatever the program. Reproducer: `def main(): i64 { return 42 }` through `zyntax compile --backend llvm -g crates/zynml/ml.zyn -s p.zynml -o p`. Fixed on branch aot-reval by 8ba7c838, which passes the entry point the CLI already resolves to set_entry_names; with it the program links and exits 42 on the NUC and the Mac. Close when that commit lands on main.","files":null}]}